findings.finding:
_overridden recomputes the fixpoint for every failing gate. The fixpoint needs one more pass over all steps for each link where a digest added late reaches an earlier step. So a check costs about O(G x n^2) for G failing gates over n steps; round 3 was linear per gate. The reviewer measured adversarial chains of trusted read-only steps, with all gates failing one subject:
- 400 pairs, 1 gate: 0.042 s;
- 1,000 pairs, 50 gates: 7.8 s;
- 1,000 pairs, 100 gates (2,101 steps): 16.3 s.
Extrapolated, not run: about 1,365 pairs with 1,365 gates fit the 4,096-step limit and would take several minutes for one trace. Each delegated child is also checked in its own right. Under the R4-1 (a) sketch the same 2,101-step trace takes 0.125 s.
